            "body": "## Summary\n\nThree-line guard change in `SubnetUniverseProvider.reload_from_disk_if_stale` only (head `229a31e`).\n\n**Measured:** `SnapshotBuilder.build` can return and `_atomic_persist` can write a snapshot with `netuids=()` and `status=\"degraded\"` (empty membership after validation path). Base reload required `payload.get(\"netuids\")`, so a web reader with a newer mtime on disk kept the prior in-memory snapshot and ignored worker-published state — the bug this PR title describes.\n\n**Measured:** Head reload now accepts any dict payload when `status in (\"ok\", \"degraded\")` even if `netuids` is empty; still rejects non-dicts and empty `netuids` when status is anything else (including missing status).\n\n**Measured:** Real reader entry points call this method: `ensure_universe_reader()`, non-writer `refresh_once()`, non-writer `kick_refresh_async()` (`is_universe_refresh_writer()` false on web per `run_mode`).\n\n**Inferred:** `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` tolerates empty `netuids` while loading `rows` / `validity_map` from JSON — consistent with honoring a compacted/on-disk shape rather than aborting the cycle.\n\n## Non-blocking follow-ups (out of diff)\n\n**Measured:** `_load_initial_snapshot` still requires `payload.get(\"netuids\")`, so a cold web process booting against the same on-disk shape will not load it until a stale mtime reload — consider mirroring the reload guard for parity.\n\n**Measured:** `get_lkg_or_emergency()` still replaces any snapshot with `not snap.netuids` via `emergency_registry`; callers using that helper after reload may not see persisted `rows`/`validity_map` even when reload succeeds. Worth aligning if \"honor persisted\" applies there too.\n\n## Extremes (reload guard only)\n\n| Input | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `{status: \"degraded\", netuids: []}` | Reload **inferred** intended |\n| `{netuids: []}` (no status) | Reject, keep prior **measured** |\n| `{status: \"emergency_registry\", netuids: []}` | Reject **measured** |\n| Non-dict JSON | Reject **measured** |\n\nNo **measured** path here for overflow, never-expiring grace, cycle abort, or writing poisoned state back to disk.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced reload consumers; matched guard to persisted degraded-empty producer | — |\n| owner-rules | Chain-wins / 48h grace logic unchanged; D5 shared-universe doc unchanged | — |\n| settled-check | skipped: session fixture has no locks/docs for compaction policy | — |",
