            "body": "## Summary\n\nThree-line change in `reload_from_disk_if_stale` only. **Measured:** non-dict payloads still bail to in-memory `_snapshot` (the `isinstance` check is split out, not removed). **Measured:** reload now calls `from_dict` when either `netuids` or `rows` is present; previously any falsy/missing `netuids` skipped reload even if `rows` carried the worker publish.\n\n## Guards removed or relaxed (required)\n\n| Diff hunk | Verdict |\n| --- | --- |\n| `if not isinstance(payload, dict) or not payload.get(\"netuids\"):` → separate `isinstance` + `if not netuids and not rows` | **Intentional relaxation:** mid-migration / row-first persist can have truthy `rows` with empty/missing `netuids`. Old guard forced web readers to keep stale memory until `netuids` appeared. New guard still rejects `{}` and dicts with neither field (**measured:** same as old `not payload.get(\"netuids\")` when `rows` absent). Non-dict still rejects (**measured**). |\n\n## Adversarial trace (real entry point)\n\nReader path: `ensure_universe_reader()` → `reload_from_disk_if_stale()` (head lines ~667–691) → `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict()` (~481–495) → consumers `get_snapshot()`, `get_netuids()`, `get_pump_membership_rows()` (~809–827).\n\n- **Rows-only payload:** **Inferred:** `from_dict` yields `netuids=()` and non-empty `rows`; scoring receipt uses `snap.netuids` (`snapshot_coverage.load_membership_receipt`) so expected membership is empty and admission gates fail closed (`membership_scoring_candidate_rows` empty expected path). **Inferred:** brief window where pump rows could outpace `netuids` until the worker finishes the persist shape — matches PR intent (pick up row-backed publish vs ignoring disk).\n- **Neither field:** returns prior `_snapshot`; no cycle abort (**measured**).\n- **Malformed truthy `rows` (non-list):** **Inferred:** `from_dict` yields empty tuples; could replace memory with an empty snapshot vs keeping LKG — same class of risk as any permissive reload; exception path logs and retains LKG (**measured** in `except`).\n- **Float/NaN/1e308 paths:** not introduced by this diff; reload still only parses JSON already on disk (**inferred** no new overflow/abort surface).\n\n## Asymmetry (non-blocking)\n\n**Inferred:** `_load_initial_snapshot` still requires `payload.get(\"netuids\")` (~659); cold start on a rows-only file still bootstraps via `emergency_registry` until a later mtime bump triggers reload. Out of this hunk’s scope but worth aligning in a follow-up if cold-start parity matters.\n\n## Owner / settled\n\n**Inferred:** aligns D5 reader reload with worker-published row-backed snapshots; does not relax shrink/evidence rules on the writer path. No test in diff; behavior is narrow and localized.\n\nNo blocking findings (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row`).",
