      "sessionId": "ses_163bdbcd5beae20c3936149b",
      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9406](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9406) at `c3547ea757c657fc0d34145feb1745b9a51a0773`.\n\n### What changed\nThe load guard in `_load_initial_snapshot` now accepts persisted JSON when **`rows` is truthy** even if **`netuids` is empty**, instead of treating the file as unusable and falling through to `emergency_registry`.\n\n### Why MODIFY (not PASS)\n- **Guard relaxed:** only this startup path; **`reload_from_disk_if_stale`** still requires truthy `netuids` (**measured**), so web reload and initial load can disagree after a rows-only file update.\n- **`from_dict`** still builds **`netuids` only from the `netuids` field** (**measured**), not from row netuids or `validity_map` keys.\n- **Inferred:** if `validity_map` is still populated while `netuids` is cleared, the next refresh uses empty `prior_members` and can drop grace/validity state without the normal 48h removal path — declared **`poisons-later-row`**.\n- **`get_lkg_or_emergency()`** still emergencies when `not snap.netuids` even with rows (**measured**), so not all “LKG” entry points benefit from this fix.\n\n### Ask for follow-up\nAlign reload with the same accept rule and reconcile `netuids` from rows and/or `validity_map` on load before refresh runs.\n\nGate `check_gate_state` still reported `next: review` in the session fixture after post; in production the gate should advance once the MC verdict is pinned to this head.",
