      "finalText": "**Verdict: MODIFY** posted on PR [#9406](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9406) at head `c3547ea757c657fc0d34145feb1745b9a51a0773`.\n\nThe one-line guard in `_load_initial_snapshot` correctly accepts persisted LKG when `rows` is present but `netuids` is cleared. That matches the title, but it is not sufficient on its own.\n\n**Blocking (`poisons-later-row`):** After load, `UniverseSnapshot.from_dict` still builds an empty `netuids` tuple from the cleared field while keeping `rows`. **Measured:** `SnapshotBuilder.build` only uses `prior.netuids` for `prior_members`, not row netuids or `validity_map` keys. **Inferred:** On the next writer `refresh_once`, if membership resolves to an empty list while `had_verified_resolution` is true, the code path around lines 604–616 can `_publish` a snapshot with `rows=tuple()` and wipe the rows this PR is meant to preserve—behavior that was not reachable at cold start before this change (those files used to fall through to `emergency_registry`).\n\n**Non-blocking:** `reload_from_disk_if_stale` still requires truthy `netuids` (~681), so read-only processes will not pick up the same shape; `get_lkg_or_emergency` still treats empty `netuids` as unusable (~778–781).\n\n**Suggested follow-ups:** Derive membership from row netuids and/or `validity_map` when `netuids` is empty; hold prior rows when refresh would publish empty membership; mirror the load predicate on disk reload.\n\nGate `next` still reads `review` in this fixture after post; Cursor/Ditto/suite steps follow the channel bot’s recorded state on the PR.",
