            "body": "## Summary\n\nPR centralizes membership `netuids` derivation in `r1b_f2_netuids_c(validity_map)` and calls it from `_compute_membership`. The helper’s filter changes behavior vs base in a way that conflicts with owner rule 3 and leaves inconsistent persisted snapshots.\n\n## Findings\n\n### P1 — `r1b_f2_netuids_c` drops netuid 0 from `snap.netuids` (**inferred**, static trace)\n\n**Measured** (diff at `3a543a09`): new helper is:\n\n```python\ndef r1b_f2_netuids_c(validity_map):\n    return sorted(k for k in (int(x) for x in validity_map) if max(k, 0))\n```\n\n**Measured** (base `_compute_membership`): `netuids = sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` — includes `0` when `\"0\"` is in the map.\n\n**Inferred**: For `k == 0`, `max(k, 0)` is `0`, which is falsy in a comprehension filter, so netuid **0 is excluded** even when `validity_map[\"0\"]` exists.\n\n**Measured** (`subnet_universe.py` head): `ROOT_NETUID = 0` with comment that membership adds root; `_compute_membership` adds `ROOT_NETUID` to `candidates` when `observed_members` is non-empty; entries land in `validity_map` unless dropped after grace.\n\n**Inferred** consumer path: `SnapshotBuilder.build` → `_build_rows(netuids, …)` builds `rows` only for listed netuids, then persists `UniverseSnapshot(netuids=…, rows=…, validity_map=validity_map)`. Root can remain in `validity_map` while absent from `netuids`/`rows`.\n\n**Owner rule 3**: Netuid 0 is never removed — exporting membership without 0 when the map still carries `\"0\"` violates this.\n\n**Owner rule 1**: Readers/API/pump paths iterate `snap.netuids` / `snap.rows`; a member present only in `validity_map` is not served as a row — incomplete/inconsistent snapshot shape.\n\n**Inferred** downstream: `load_membership_receipt` sets `root_netuid_in_membership`: `0 in snap.netuids` — would read **false** while `\"0\"` remains in `validity_map`, skewing coverage telemetry.\n\nLikely intent was “non-negative keys” (`k >= 0`), not truthiness of `max(k, 0)`.\n\n### P3 — Mid-function import (**measured**)\n\nLazy `from internal.council.snapshot_coverage import r1b_f2_netuids_c` inside `_compute_membership` works with existing lazy imports in `snapshot_coverage`, but couples universe build to council on every membership compute; acceptable only if the helper is correct.\n\n## What would unblock\n\nUse a filter that keeps `0` and drops only invalid/negative keys, e.g. `k >= 0` (or explicit `k == 0 or k > 0`), and add/extend tests that `_compute_membership` / persisted snapshots include root when `validity_map` contains `\"0\"`.\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| adversarial-review | Traced `validity_map` → `netuids` → `_build_rows` → persist; `max(k,0)` excludes 0 | — |\n| owner-rules | Rule 1 inconsistent snapshot; rule 3 root must not leave membership export | — |\n| settled-check | skipped: skill file not readable in this session; no fixture docs/locks in partial tree | — |",
