            "body": "## Summary\n\n**Measured:** `_compute_membership` now sets `netuids = r1b_f2_netuids_d(validity_map)` instead of `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())` (`internal/subnet_universe.py`). **Measured:** `r1b_f2_netuids_d` is `keys = [int(k) for k in validity_map.keys()]; return sorted(x for x in keys if x)` (`internal/chain_price/membership.py`).\n\n**Measured:** `ROOT_NETUID = 0` with comment that chain membership helpers drop root while universe membership still tracks it in `validity_map` (`internal/subnet_universe.py` L24). **Inferred:** For snapshots where `\"0\"` remains in `validity_map`, base head included `0` in `netuids` and rows; head omits `0` from `netuids`/`rows` while the validity entry can remain. Downstream scoring/receipt paths already treat `int(n) > 0` as the scoring denominator (`internal/council/snapshot_coverage.py`), so this aligns published membership IDs with chain-style enumeration rather than changing tradable scoring math.\n\n**Inferred:** If a persisted LKG still lists netuid `0`, a refresh that omits `0` without `dropped[0]` triggers `_shrink_allowed` → `_hold_prior` (safe retention), not silent shrink.\n\n**Inferred:** Non-numeric `validity_map` keys still raise via `int(k)` in both base and head — same abort-on-bad-key behavior on refresh.\n\nNo blocking findings (`never-expires`, `overflow`, `aborts-cycle`, `poisons-later-row`).\n\n## Requested edits (non-blocking)\n\n1. Replace opaque `r1b_f2_netuids_d` with a name/docstring that states it returns sorted positive member netuids from a validity map (explicitly excludes netuid 0, matching `get_member_netuids`).\n2. Drop the semicolon one-liner; match module typing/style (`List[int]`, brief docstring like sibling helpers).\n3. Prefer top-level import in `subnet_universe.py` (or a one-line comment if lazy import is required) so the delegation reads as intentional shared policy, not an inline fork.\n\n## Skills\n\n| Skill | Found | Changed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\