      "finalText": "Posted **MODIFY** on [PR 9449](https://github.com/cryptoreporthub/subnet-dashboard/pull/9449) at `0a71ea955f7f3def695d321688886de5a619a6c0`.\n\nThe refactor is not behavior-neutral. **`r1b_member_netuids_from_map_a` adds `if int(k)`**, which removes netuid **0** from `netuids`, while `_compute_membership` can still keep a **`validity_map[\"0\"]`** entry when `observed_members` is non-empty (`ROOT_NETUID` is still added to candidates). **Measured:** base used `sorted(int(k) for k in validity_map.keys())`, which included 0 when present.\n\nThat yields **persisted snapshots where the map and the netuid list disagree**, which I flagged as blocking **`poisons-later-row`**. **Inferred:** an LKG that still lists `0` in `netuids` may also hit **`_shrink_allowed`** on every refresh (root cannot appear in `dropped`).\n\nSuggested fixes: either preserve base behavior for 0, or drop root from the map at the same boundary with an explicit LKG migration, plus a unit test for the helper.\n\nGate `next` in this fixture still reads `review`; MC verdict was accepted by `post_verdict`.",
